});
``

Wait, `.map(...)` is lazy and single-iteration — use `.toList()`. Or build strings first. Let me restructure:

```dart
final base36Chars = [
 for (var i = 0; i < 10; i++) String.fromCharCode(0x30 + i),
 for (var i = 0; i < 26; i++) String.fromCharCode(0x61 + i),
];
for (final a in base36Chars) {
 for (final b in base36Chars) {
   final minted = '$prefix$a$b';
   ...
 }
``

So I no longer need the `_base36` const in the helper at all — bump by code units. Cleaner and immune to the redactor. Both files.

Note this also means my helper docs referencing "alphabet successor" stay accurate.

Also — the failure was caught by my own sweep test, which is nice TDD synergy, but the root was a tool-layer artifact, not code logic. Fix both files now.

